---
args: {"portfolio": "HandoverPortfolio", "reply": "SuccessorAcknowledgment"}
returns: "TransferReplyReview"
---
1. Find slice by reply.sliceKey in portfolio.slices. Verify reply identity, expectedPortfolioRevision, exact scope, signer and successor authority from reply.authorityAndReplyEvidence. For a stale revision return TransferReplyReview { portfolio, outcome: "stale", acceptedSliceKeys: [], remainingUnownedKeys: the still-unowned slice keys, questions: the actual intervening slice changes }. Missing slice, authority or ambiguous scope returns the same unchanged portfolio with outcome unresolved and precise questions.
2. If reply.id was already consumed, compare its authority/source identity and the stored slice acceptance against the supplied scope and checkpoint. An identical replay returns the existing accepted and unowned keys with no state change; conflicting reuse returns unresolved. Do not accept a new scope merely because the reply ID is familiar.
3. Bind partitions = partitionAcknowledgedScope(slice, reply). Require a complete non-overlapping partition of the original scope. A discrepancy returns the unchanged portfolio and an unresolved question. Keep unmentioned or declined work explicitly unowned and confirm nextCheckpoint only when the actual reply establishes it.
4. Bind nextPortfolio as HandoverPortfolio { revision: portfolio.revision + 1, promises: portfolio.promises, progress: portfolio.progress, prerequisites: portfolio.prerequisites, slices: replace only this exact slice with partitions while preserving all other slices and original promise attribution, introductions: portfolio.introductions, capture: portfolio.capture, replyIds: portfolio.replyIds plus reply.id once }. Return TransferReplyReview { portfolio: nextPortfolio, outcome: "accepted-slice", acceptedSliceKeys: the evidenced accepted partition keys, remainingUnownedKeys: all residual unowned keys, questions: remaining scope or checkpoint questions }. A successor acceptance does not assert completion of the underlying work.
